From: Arkadiusz Miśkiewicz <arekm@maven.pl>
Date: Thu Nov 19 15:33:37 2026 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Do not leak stored HTTP response header lines

The 5.4 port of the folded header parser copies every stored response
header into $http_response_header and never frees its own buffer, so
each header leaks until the end of the request; a long running script
fetching URLs grows without bound. Hand the buffer over to the zval,
as 8.x does with ZVAL_NEW_STR().
PLD: PLD fix for the 5.4 port of the GHSA-v8xr-gpvj-cx9g folding fix
---
diff --git a/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c b/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
--- a/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
+++ b/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
@@ -374,7 +374,7 @@ static zend_bool php_stream_http_response_headers_parse(php_stream_wrapper *wrap
 		zval *http_response;
 
 		MAKE_STD_ZVAL(http_response);
-		ZVAL_STRINGL(http_response, last_header_line_str, last_header_line_length, 1);
+		ZVAL_STRINGL(http_response, last_header_line_str, last_header_line_length, 0);
 		zend_hash_next_index_insert(Z_ARRVAL_P(response_header), &http_response, sizeof(zval *), NULL);
 	} else {
 		efree(last_header_line_str);
